{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"callout","kind":"caution","title":"Caution","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You don't need to call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defer"},{"type":"text","value":" manually anymore, Promises are handled automatically now."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defer"},{"type":"text","value":" function wraps a promise with a deferred state object that can be used to inspect the promise's state. This deferred promise can then be passed to the "},{"type":"link","href":"./useAwaitedHook.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAwaited"}]},{"type":"text","value":" hook or the "},{"type":"link","href":"./awaitComponent.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Await>"}]},{"type":"text","value":" component for suspending until the promise is resolved or rejected."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defer"},{"type":"text","value":" function accepts a single argument, the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"promise"},{"type":"text","value":" to wrap with a deferred state object."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"defer-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"defer options"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Promise<T>"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The promise to wrap with a deferred state object."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"defer-returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"defer returns"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A promise that can be passed to the "},{"type":"link","href":"./useAwaitedHook.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useAwaited"}]},{"type":"text","value":" hook or the "},{"type":"link","href":"./awaitComponent.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"<Await>"}]},{"type":"text","value":" component."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { defer } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst route = createRoute({\n  loader: () => {\n    const deferredPromise = defer(fetch('/api/data'))\n    return { deferredPromise }\n  },\n  component: MyComponent,\n})\n\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const { deferredPromise } = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n  const data = useAwaited({ promise: deferredPromise })\n\n  // or\n\n  return (\n    <Await promise={deferredPromise}>\n      {(data) => <div>{JSON.stringify(data)}</div>}\n    </Await>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"defer-options","text":"defer options","level":2},{"id":"defer-returns","text":"defer returns","level":2},{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n> [!CAUTION]\n> You don't need to call `defer` manually anymore, Promises are handled automatically now.\n\nThe `defer` function wraps a promise with a deferred state object that can be used to inspect the promise's state. This deferred promise can then be passed to the [`useAwaited`](./useAwaitedHook.md) hook or the [`<Await>`](./awaitComponent.md) component for suspending until the promise is resolved or rejected.\n\nThe `defer` function accepts a single argument, the `promise` to wrap with a deferred state object.\n\n## defer options\n\n- Type: `Promise<T>`\n- Required\n- The promise to wrap with a deferred state object.\n\n## defer returns\n\n- A promise that can be passed to the [`useAwaited`](./useAwaitedHook.md) hook or the [`<Await>`](./awaitComponent.md) component.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { defer } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst route = createRoute({\n  loader: () => {\n    const deferredPromise = defer(fetch('/api/data'))\n    return { deferredPromise }\n  },\n  component: MyComponent,\n})\n\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const { deferredPromise } = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n  const data = useAwaited({ promise: deferredPromise })\n\n  // or\n\n  return (\n    <Await promise={deferredPromise}>\n      {(data) => <div>{JSON.stringify(data)}</div>}\n    </Await>\n  )\n}\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: deferFunction\ntitle: defer function\n---\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> You don't need to call `defer` manually anymore, Promises are handled automatically now.\n\nThe `defer` function wraps a promise with a deferred state object that can be used to inspect the promise's state. This deferred promise can then be passed to the [`useAwaited`](./useAwaitedHook.md) hook or the [`<Await>`](./awaitComponent.md) component for suspending until the promise is resolved or rejected.\n\nThe `defer` function accepts a single argument, the `promise` to wrap with a deferred state object.\n\n## defer options\n\n- Type: `Promise<T>`\n- Required\n- The promise to wrap with a deferred state object.\n\n## defer returns\n\n- A promise that can be passed to the [`useAwaited`](./useAwaitedHook.md) hook or the [`<Await>`](./awaitComponent.md) component.\n\n## Examples\n\n```tsx\nimport { defer } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst route = createRoute({\n  loader: () => {\n    const deferredPromise = defer(fetch('/api/data'))\n    return { deferredPromise }\n  },\n  component: MyComponent,\n})\n\nfunction MyComponent() {\n  const { deferredPromise } = Route.useLoaderData()\n\n  const data = useAwaited({ promise: deferredPromise })\n\n  // or\n\n  return (\n    <Await promise={deferredPromise}>\n      {(data) => <div>{JSON.stringify(data)}</div>}\n    </Await>\n  )\n}\n```\n"}
